<template>
    <SiteShell page="workflow">
        <div class="page-head">
            <span class="kicker">Pipeline</span>
            <h1>How a film becomes an MP4</h1>
            <p class="lead">
                Authoring, evaluation, preflight, rasterization, sound and
                encoding are separate stages with one owner each. No stage is
                allowed to quietly skip another.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pipe" aria-label="Render pipeline">
            <span>TypeScript DSL</span>
            <span class="pipe__arrow">→</span>
            <span>scene IR</span>
            <span class="pipe__arrow">→</span>
            <span>motion + preflight</span>
            <span class="pipe__arrow">→</span>
            <span>raster · text · audio</span>
            <span class="pipe__arrow">→</span>
            <span>H.264 / AAC</span>
            <span class="pipe__arrow">→</span>
            <span class="pipe__end">MP4</span>
        </div>

        <ol class="steps">
            <li>
                <h2>Write the film</h2>
                <p>
                    Describe the canvas, the design roles and the scenes in one
                    TypeScript file. A scene is a value, not a project file.
                </p>
                <pre><code>const film = new Film({ width: 1280, height: 720 });</code></pre>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h2>Compose the scenes</h2>
                <p>
                    Items are laid out in list order inside each scene. Durations
                    and offsets are written in seconds; the binding converts to
                    frames.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h2>Animate with time windows</h2>
                <p>
                    Give an item an <code>id</code>, then attach <code>anim</code> windows and <code>follow</code> timing. Evaluation stays in
                    the shared motion stage.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h2>Add sound</h2>
                <p>
                    Grooves, melodic instruments, effects and singing are all
                    code. Narration is a PCM16 WAV mixed into its reserved slot.
                </p>
                <pre><code>film.audio({ patterns: [{ preset: 'four-on-floor', bpm: 120 }] });</code></pre>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h2>Preflight the media</h2>
                <p>
                    Required images, video and audio are resolved before the
                    encoder opens. A missing or undecodable asset stops the run
                    with a located error.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h2>Preview a frame</h2>
                <p>
                    Render a single frame to check composition, fonts and color
                    before committing to the full encode.
                </p>
                <pre><code>open-cut preview films/demo.ts --frame 90 -o dist/frame.png</code></pre>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h2>Render and trace the result</h2>
                <p>
                    Encode the whole film, then ask the binary which native
                    version and source revision produced it. The same spec and
                    seed should reproduce the same bytes.
                </p>
                <pre><code>open-cut render films/demo.ts -o dist/demo.mp4</code></pre>
                <pre><code>open-cut build</code></pre>
            </li>
        </ol>

        <section class="section">
            <h2>Where each stage lives</h2>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Stage</th>
                            <th>Owner</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Authoring</td>
                            <td>TypeScript DSL: <code>Film</code>, <code>Scene</code> and item constructors.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>IR</td>
                            <td>Neutral <code>media.scene</code> — one serializable project shape.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Motion</td>
                            <td>Neutral <code>media.motion</code> — ids, animation keys, follow windows.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Import</td>
                            <td>Neutral <code>media.codec</code> — WIC images, Media Foundation video and audio, cached per path.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Raster and text</td>
                            <td>Neutral <code>media.raster</code> + <code>media.text</code> — real font rasterization with per-glyph fallback.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Audio</td>
                            <td>Neutral <code>media.audio</code>, <code>media.synthesis</code> and <code>media.voice</code>.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Encode</td>
                            <td>Neutral <code>media.codec</code> — H.264 plus negotiated AAC or FLAC through the Media Foundation sink writer.</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <p class="cta-line">
            The repository owns the authoring surface and the binding — never a
            second renderer. What runs today is listed in the
            <Link to="RoadmapPage">roadmap</Link>.
        </p>
    </SiteShell>
</template>

